      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "NAFNet deblur, rebuilt from GENERIC cv2.dnn nodes (no CV_NafnetDeblur)\n\nThis reproduces workflow 31 WITHOUT the model-specific node, to show the pre/post-processing is just plain OpenCV. The pipeline is:\n\n  Load Image\n   -> DNN Blob From Image   (cv2.dnn.blobFromImage: scale 1/255, swap R/B, native size)\n   -> DNN Forward           (loads deblurring_nafnet_2025may.onnx, runs one forward pass)\n   -> DNN Images From Blob  (cv2.dnn.imagesFromBlob: undoes the CHW->HWC transpose)\n   -> cv2.convertScaleAbs   (alpha=255: the scale + clip to 0-255, replacing the numpy clip)\n   -> CV Array -> Image     (RGB: back to a ComfyUI IMAGE)\n\nThe three DNN nodes are GENERIC: swap in any ONNX image model (super-resolution, denoise, style transfer) and adjust the blob scale/size to match it. Note: this network needs each side >= 369 px (this image is large enough). The CV_NafnetDeblur node pads small inputs for you; this generic chain does not, on purpose - the padding is model-specific. Inference is heavy (tens of seconds for a ~1.5 MP image on CPU).\n\n(cv2.convertScaleAbs is the standard OpenCV float->uint8 scale+clip. It also takes the absolute value, which is harmless here - a deblurred image is essentially non-negative - so it matches the reference's np.clip to within a level or two on the rare near-black pixel.)"
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
